{
  "name": "iOS — Journey vs Crashes by Screen (guided)",
  "tabs": [
    {
      "name": "Guided analysis",
      "stylistic_components": [
        {
          "id": "t-intro-h",
          "text_component": {
            "text": "iOS — which journeys lead to crashes?",
            "variant": "h2"
          },
          "dashboard_layout_settings": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 0,
            "column_span": 12,
            "row_span": 3
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "t-intro-p",
          "text_component": {
            "text": "A crash CAN be the terminal node of a Sankey on iOS — but only with sessionStrategy .activityBased(). Under the default .fixed() it never closes: the crash is read on the next launch into a brand-new session, disconnected from whatever flow was mid-progress when the process died. activityBased resumes the same session across the relaunch (if it lands within inactivityThresholdMins of the crash), so the replayed crash log arrives inside the session that was already walking the flow, and it closes. See CaptureBridge.swift.",
            "variant": "p"
          },
          "dashboard_layout_settings": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 3,
            "column_span": 12,
            "row_span": 7
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "t-s1-h",
          "text_component": {
            "text": "Start here — paths that end in a crash",
            "variant": "h3"
          },
          "dashboard_layout_settings": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 10,
            "column_span": 12,
            "row_span": 3
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "t-s1-p",
          "text_component": {
            "text": "The Sankey below terminates at the actual crash, not a proxy screen. Each node's outgoing links show, for real, how many journeys through that screen continued versus crashed — read that ratio as the crash rate for that screen; it needs no separate numerator/denominator chart, and it can't go stale between windows the way a rate metric can. flow-closed-count below it is a control: if it stops moving while crashes are still happening, sessions are aging out before the relaunch lands.",
            "variant": "p"
          },
          "dashboard_layout_settings": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 13,
            "column_span": 12,
            "row_span": 7
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "t-s2-h",
          "text_component": {
            "text": "Where journeys drop off",
            "variant": "h3"
          },
          "dashboard_layout_settings": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 48,
            "column_span": 12,
            "row_span": 3
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "t-s2-p",
          "text_component": {
            "text": "Read these two together: the funnel bars are the Sankey columns, left to right. The funnel tells you how many survive each stage; the Sankey tells you which routes they took and where they branched. A stage that loses volume in the funnel AND has a high crash rate above is a crash-driven leak; losing volume with a near-zero crash rate is UX, not crashes.",
            "variant": "p"
          },
          "dashboard_layout_settings": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 51,
            "column_span": 12,
            "row_span": 5
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "t-s3-h",
          "text_component": {
            "text": "Raw crash detail",
            "variant": "h3"
          },
          "dashboard_layout_settings": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 82,
            "column_span": 12,
            "row_span": 3
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "t-s3-p",
          "text_component": {
            "text": "Counts by the screen the user was on when the previous run died, reported next launch from a persisted field — which is how it catches hangs and OOM kills. Filter reason to fatalCrash for real crashes. 'other' means the app died before reaching any screen.",
            "variant": "p"
          },
          "dashboard_layout_settings": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 85,
            "column_span": 12,
            "row_span": 4
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "t-how-h",
          "text_component": {
            "text": "Caveats",
            "variant": "h3"
          },
          "dashboard_layout_settings": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 101,
            "column_span": 12,
            "row_span": 3
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "t-how-p",
          "text_component": {
            "text": "Correlational, not causal. Attribution is to the last screen reached, so a background crash still lands on whatever was visible. The Sankey closing depends on the relaunch landing within inactivityThresholdMins (30 min default) of the crash — a slow relaunch ages the session out and you're back to the .fixed()-style empty Sankey.",
            "variant": "p"
          },
          "dashboard_layout_settings": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 104,
            "column_span": 12,
            "row_span": 4
          }
        }
      ],
